<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21160" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hypaethrus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-os</span></b> , a, um, adj., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπαιθρος</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that is in the open air</i>, <i>uncovered.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Adj.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ambulationes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vitr. 5,
					9 <i>med.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">loca (with aperta),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
				ib.</span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Subst.
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hy-paethros</span></b> , i,
				m., <i>a temple open</i> or <i>without roof</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 3, 2,
				1</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hypaethrum</span></b> , i,
				n., <i>an open building</i>, <i><span class="en">Dig. 33, 7, 12, § 20</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. 50, 16, 242, §
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hypaethra</span></b> ,
				ōrum, n., <i>uncovered</i>, <i>open walks</i>, <i><span class="en">Vitr. 1,
			2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
